Corresponding source / how to rebuild
-------------------------------------
The complete corresponding source is the directory gsi/apps/Z9xAirPlay (AndroidManifest.xml,
res/, assets/, src/, jni/ with glue/, patches/ and build scripts) plus the unmodified
third-party trees gsi/apps/third_party/{UxPlay,libplist,boringssl,alac} at the commits above,
gsi/apps/build_apk.sh and gsi/apps/i18n (translations: gen.py + langs/). Exact versions,
flags and checksums: jni/BUILDINFO.txt.

Build inputs (offline, macOS or Linux shell):
  - Android NDK r29 (29.0.14206865)                 native library
  - Android SDK build-tools 36.0.0 (aapt2, d8, zipalign, apksigner) and platform android-34
  - JDK 21 (17 also works)
  - build_apk.sh's HEADERS_JAR (default gsi/apps/sdk/framework-full-headers.jar: the
    compile-time header jar of the image's framework, built from the LineageOS 21 tree).
    Z9xAirPlay uses only public SDK APIs, so HEADERS_JAR=<sdk>/platforms/android-34/android.jar
    builds the same app.
  - signing key: KEY_PK8 / KEY_PEM (default gsi/apps/sdk/platform.*, the image's platform key)

From the directory that contains gsi/:
  sh gsi/apps/Z9xAirPlay/jni/build_native.sh            # -> Z9xAirPlay/lib/<abi>/, BUILDINFO.txt
  BUILD_DIR="$PWD/gsi/apps/Z9xAirPlay/build/apk" VERSION_CODE=1 VERSION_NAME=1.0 \
    sh gsi/apps/build_apk.sh gsi/apps/Z9xAirPlay gsi/apps/out/Z9xAirPlay.apk
(BUILD_DIR keeps build_apk.sh from wiping Z9xAirPlay/build, which also holds the native
build cache.)

